;; spec:   stdlib §2.5, §8.1 item 5 (count cases)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 3
;; audit:  clean
;; allocs: <= 10
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: vec
;; The price of the bulk builder is a constant. vec of an Array of three elements allocates 10 objects;
;; the conj loop that was the default allocated 8 (measured with the compiler built before the
;; builder: 4 for one element, 6 for two, 8 for three, 10 for four, 12 for five), and the builder's
;; 10 is the same for one to four elements and 9 at 32, so a vector of one to three elements
;; costs more than it did, of four the same, of five or more less (case 483: 64 elements, 15 against
;; 133). The case pins the 10 so that a change to the constant is seen: a cheaper builder fails
;; the bound until it is lowered, a dearer one fails it at once, and the harness's own test lowers it
;; by one and requires the failure.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll))

(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((v (vec (array 3 0))))
    (count v)))
